Copy this directory to a working directory and revise the example files for each run.

Local workstation examples:
  config_eg.py
  1.1_parallel_pick_assoc_eg.py
  1.2_parallel_assoc_eg.py

SCEDC AWS archive examples:
  config_aws_eg.py
  1.1_parallel_pick_aws_eg.py
  1.2_parallel_assoc_aws_eg.py

The AWS examples use these source modules from the parent 1_PAL directory:
  data_pipeline_aws.py
  run_pick_aws.py
  run_assoc_aws.py

Place the full AWS picking station file at input/example_aws_pal.csv. Place
subnet station files at input/example_aws_pal_r1.csv, input/example_aws_pal_r2.csv,
and so forth. Revise all paths, dates, worker counts, AWS settings, and output
names near the beginning of each copied executable.

The AWS example date range uses an exclusive end date. For example,
20250101-20250102 processes archive day 2025-01-01.
